  "releaseNotes": "- [ThunderPropagator#26] [Critical] Receive loop started with CancellationToken.None — not linked to host lifetime   Root cause across all 5 files: Each ReceiveAsync implementation created a new CancellationTokenSource inside a using block, then passed the CTS token to ChannelManager.Receive — which is   fire-and-forget. By the time ReceiveAsync returned, the using block disposed the CTS, leaving the background task holding a token from a disposed source. Meanwhile, the cancellationToken parameter    of ReceiveAsync was already properly linked to ApplicationStopping (via AbstractConnectionHandler._receivingCts) and never disposed prematurely.",
